    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions of the road.\n• Keep the access drive clear of parked vehicles to allow fire apparatus to reach the residence without obstruction.\n• Create a turnaround area near the residence or detached structure large enough for emergency vehicles to reverse direction without backing out to the road.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along the access drive to maintain overhead and side clearance for emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back dense vegetation growing close to the main residence and detached structure to open a clear path around both buildings for responders on foot.\n• Thin dense vegetation between the road and the structures so responders can see the buildings and assess conditions on approach.\n• Keep a clear walking path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between the two buildings quickly."
