    "recommendations": "• Trim back shrubs and low branches that are directly touching or leaning against the house walls.\n• Clear ground vegetation within several feet of the foundation on all sides of the house.\n• Thin the tree cluster nearest the structure to create open space between individual trees and between the trees and the house.\n• Remove shrubs growing beneath trees near the house to reduce the connection between ground-level plants and tree canopy.\n• Cut back or remove brush in the dense brush area closest to the structure.\n• Thin scattered shrubs around the house so they are separated from each other and from the building.\n• Clear vegetation growing along both edges of the driveway so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Trim overhanging tree branches above the driveway to maintain overhead clearance for emergency vehicles.\n• Remove dead or dry ground vegetation along the driveway that could carry fire toward the house.\n• Keep the area between tree clusters and the structure open by removing shrubs and ground cover that connect them.\n• Thin mixed vegetation on the sides of the house where plants are densest to create visible open gaps around the building.\n• Maintain the open terrain areas by preventing shrub or brush encroachment toward the structure over time."
